Ok Guys, let's start.


Purpose:
--------

 -First Door:
 ------------

First of all i would like to say that this Door was written because there are
so many Status-Doors out there which dont show the right kind of thing.The
first shows only a few things, which could be important, but not all of those
kind of Doors have this things.The second thing i dont like is the rating
which is choosen by someone who could be really mad.This Door makes it poss-
ible to show the User which is using this Door which Commands are available
for him.He will shown a Text-File wich shows him all available Commands.The 
only thng is that the Sysop have to Edit it.Further Explaination follows at
the Installation
This Time i changed the Door from AIM to XIM Door because its much faster than
Arexx. Ok try it out.

 -Second Door:
 -------------

Yes! There is a second Door!! Do you see the shit Status which is shown by
/X 2.xx and /X 3.xx. I saw a Status in the fine S-Express so i decided to 
write a similar one for /X-Users. So try it and enjoy it!

Installation:
-------------

First of all it is an XIM-Door which could be used in /X2.xx & /X3.xx

 - Installation on /X 2.xx:
 --------------------------

The Installation on /X2.xx is to be like the following:
First of all copy all files of the Door-Directory in this Archive to Yours
and then add the following lines to your BBSCMD:

-------^Cut here^-----------------------
S         XM010DOORS:PIWI/STATUSBBS
-------^and here^-----------------------

The Installation of the second Door is only to add a Command to your SYSCMD
because the File which is needed is in the Door-Directory too. So just add
following Lines to Your SYSCMD:

-------^Cut here^-----------------------
S         XM010DOORS:PIWI/STATUSSYS
-------^and here^-----------------------

Ok the next thing you have to do is to edit a Textfile which contains all
the Commands to the Security-Level someone has
I.e.:Edit the File Access(Access-Level) --> Access200
     This File must contain all available Commands for Security-Level
Thats all Folks.

 - Installation on /X 3.xx:
 --------------------------

The Installation for /X3.xx-Users is much easier to handle. Just copy the
complete Door-irectory to yours and copy all the Commands to yours. Be sure
that BOTH, either the bbscmd- AND the syscmd-Command-Infos are copied.
Ok the next thing you have to do is to edit a Textfile which contains all
the Commands to the Security-Level someone has
I.e.:Edit the File Access(Access-Level) --> Access200
     This File must contain all available Commands for Security-Level

Thats all for doing  under /X3.xx


History:
--------


V0.1 First only Internal Release, Bugs in Formatting the Output
     Never released

V0.2 Bugs in Formatting removed, added some Kind of Color-Formatting
     Never released too

V0.5 All Kind of Formatting corrected and building some colors in output.
     Released: 15-04-94

V0.6 Some Bugs Fixed; Sorry you cant use any Other BBS-Name than 'BAD RELIGION' - Bug fixed ;
     Some cosmetical Changes made
     Released: 18-04-94
V1.0 Some Additional work done, compiled in C-Language, able to show all 
     available Commands at Security-Level which someone has
	 Released: 05-05-94

